### Registration flow: scan_cdf -> DeltaCdfTableProvider -> ctx.register_table

Source: https://github.com/delta-io/delta-rs/blob/main/crates/core/src/operations/load_cdf.rs

End-to-end test snippet showing how to build a CdfLoadBuilder with explicit starting version, wrap it in DeltaCdfTableProvider, and register it as a DataFusion table for SQL querying.

```rust
let table = DeltaTable::try_from_url(table_uri).await?;

let builder = table.scan_cdf().with_starting_version(0);
let provider = DeltaCdfTableProvider::try_new(builder)?;
ctx.register_table("cdf", Arc::new(provider))?;

let df = ctx
    .sql("SELECT * FROM cdf WHERE birthday = DATE '2023-12-25'")
    .await?;
```

### Querying Delta Tables > Rust API with Datafusion

Source: https://github.com/delta-io/delta-rs/blob/main/docs/usage/querying-delta-tables.md

When using the Rust API, Apache Datafusion can be employed to query data from a Delta table. This involves registering the table with a `SessionContext` and then using SQL queries or the Dataframe interface to filter and select data.
